WEBVTT

00:04.140 --> 00:07.360
<i>What is this, a dream?</i>

00:10.180 --> 00:12.610
<i>That's right, a dream.</i>

00:12.990 --> 00:14.500
<i>Of course it's a dream. </i>

00:16.480 --> 00:21.370
<i>A bad dream, just a bad dream! </i>

00:41.140 --> 00:47.860
Shining stars away bless

00:41.680 --> 00:47.860
Shining stars away bless

00:48.190 --> 00:53.070
chiisakutonaeru mahou no kotobawa

00:48.190 --> 00:53.070
Silently chanting the magical words

00:53.950 --> 00:55.700
『onegai。。。』

00:53.950 --> 00:55.700
"please"

00:55.990 --> 01:01.330
hoshizora samayou kaze ni notta maigo notsubu

00:55.990 --> 01:01.330
The lost grain riding the wind on the sky

01:01.330 --> 01:02.370
『kizuite。。。』

01:01.330 --> 01:02.370
Please notice

01:02.370 --> 01:10.250
tsutawara nakute porori ochita kono omoi

01:02.370 --> 01:10.250
Untold words, teardrops of feelings that fell down

01:10.750 --> 01:17.340
kagayaki dasuyo GARASU bin nonaka

01:10.750 --> 01:17.340
Show your shine inside the glass bottle

01:17.720 --> 01:24.730
manten no hoshi deatta KISEKI kimi ga soba ni itekureru nara

01:17.720 --> 01:24.730
If you will stay beside me perfect star of encountered miracles...

01:24.890 --> 01:32.110
Whatever the mystery, I will be able to gather my courage.

01:25.310 --> 01:32.110
donna fushigi mouke tomeru yuuki umare te yuku yo

01:32.440 --> 01:39.700
nanatsuiro ni hikaru houseki sora kara mai oriru

01:32.440 --> 01:39.700
Seven colored glittering gems flying down from the sky

01:39.700 --> 01:43.410
Scoop up the important fragments

01:40.120 --> 01:43.410
daijina KAKERA sukui agerune

01:43.410 --> 01:48.920
kowasa nuyou sotto。。。

01:43.410 --> 01:48.920
And secretly hold onto them tight

01:56.430 --> 02:01.170
<i>The worst part about dreaming is the moment you wake up.</i>

02:01.950 --> 02:03.760
<i>It's supposed to be that way.</i>

02:04.260 --> 02:07.520
<i>Open your eyes, don't do anything and settle down.  </i>

02:08.310 --> 02:12.420
<i>Nothing will change. It's just a normal room. </i>

02:40.090 --> 02:43.030
Calm down, this is just a dream!

02:43.030 --> 02:45.030
Huh, a dream?

02:45.030 --> 02:45.930
Yes.

02:55.840 --> 02:57.910
<i>What am I doing? </i>

02:59.530 --> 03:03.440
Hydrangea Colored Memories

03:07.770 --> 03:09.640
A normal morning.

03:10.340 --> 03:12.410
Nothing different from yesterday.

03:13.740 --> 03:19.240
Was the sheep doll, the star drops and everything just a dream?

03:19.240 --> 03:19.980
Yo, Haru.

03:20.500 --> 03:21.770
Morning!

03:21.770 --> 03:26.450
Then why was I sleeping in Akihime's room?

03:27.930 --> 03:30.140
You never change, Tsuwabuki.

03:30.830 --> 03:34.060
Hey, Haru. I heard you joined the Gardening Club. Is that true?

03:34.470 --> 03:36.570
Huh? Kinda.

03:36.840 --> 03:40.090
I never knew you liked gardening...

03:40.090 --> 03:41.300
Well, that's...

03:41.300 --> 03:42.460
Ah, Nako-san.

03:42.460 --> 03:43.570
Good morning, Sumomo-chan.

03:45.900 --> 03:46.530
Morning.

04:00.890 --> 04:05.030
<i>I wonder why Akihime is different at school. </i>

04:11.440 --> 04:14.870
Well it's fine since I returned to my old self.

04:19.730 --> 04:24.050
Eh? Uwahhh!

04:29.150 --> 04:31.910
G-Guess it's going to be like this...

04:31.910 --> 04:34.830
Yep, that's how it's going to be indeed.

04:38.520 --> 04:42.110
In the morning as the sun comes up, you go back to your human body.

04:42.240 --> 04:44.900
When the day is over, you will be back to your doll body.

04:45.130 --> 04:47.340
It's an easy rule to understand.

04:47.340 --> 04:49.210
So it's like that...

04:49.210 --> 04:56.370
That, and the transformation effect in Figurare has a connection with the moon phase.

04:56.980 --> 04:58.520
The moon phase?

04:58.870 --> 05:02.400
For example during the new moon, you will not transform.

05:02.400 --> 05:04.620
You will stay your human form for the whole day.

05:04.620 --> 05:08.690
But watch out, during the opposite phase, full moon, you will stay as a doll the whole day.

05:08.690 --> 05:10.030
Why?!

05:10.700 --> 05:13.620
Like I said, it's the moon effect.

05:15.650 --> 05:18.360
Well then, Tsuwabuki-kun.

05:18.800 --> 05:21.000
Tonight you will go to the Stellar Spinear's side again.

05:22.740 --> 05:24.800
By the way, one more thing...

05:25.060 --> 05:28.410
Don't let anyone see you taking the star drops, okay?!

05:29.840 --> 05:33.600
Otherwise, it will become really complicated.

05:40.340 --> 05:42.180
I'm flying...

05:43.790 --> 05:45.220
Alright!

05:52.290 --> 05:53.990
Err...

05:54.200 --> 05:57.500
Uwahh, it's so cute!

06:00.180 --> 06:02.970
It just came in today.

06:04.890 --> 06:08.000
<i>This is a uniform I made a long time ago. </i>

06:08.000 --> 06:10.800
<i>Now Sumomo, I think it will fit you perfectly. </i>

06:10.800 --> 06:12.680
<i>It will look nice on you.</i>

06:12.680 --> 06:14.030
<i>From... Mother.</i>

06:15.400 --> 06:20.310
Even though she's overseas, Mom always thinks of you everyday, Sumomo.

06:21.930 --> 06:24.900
Thank you, Mom.

06:24.900 --> 06:28.620
Well then, I'll go finish writing my manuscript.

06:29.170 --> 06:31.460
Deadlines, deadlines...

06:31.460 --> 06:32.740
Okay.

06:33.330 --> 06:36.500
So Akihime's father is a novel writer?

06:37.430 --> 06:39.820
And her mother is overseas.

07:03.190 --> 07:04.590
Yuki-chan.

07:06.960 --> 07:10.540
Where did you go? You were gone this morning.

07:10.540 --> 07:14.370
I thought Yuki-chan and the star drops were just a dream.

07:14.860 --> 07:16.800
I can't breathe...

07:16.800 --> 07:22.480
It seems that I can only come here during the night.

07:23.160 --> 07:24.550
I see.

07:24.550 --> 07:30.260
Also, we shouldn't let anyone see us when we're using magic.

07:30.260 --> 07:32.120
Okay! Then...

07:33.600 --> 07:35.370
Cute!

07:35.370 --> 07:37.670
You look so cute, Yuki-chan.

07:41.710 --> 07:44.960
Looking good! All of them look lovely.

07:45.400 --> 07:50.140
As I thought, compared to her at school, she looks more lively at home.

07:52.360 --> 07:54.240
Yep, let's use this one.

07:54.710 --> 07:57.240
Am I a cow now?

07:59.520 --> 08:00.820
It's here!

08:00.820 --> 08:02.430
It's the star drop.

08:09.980 --> 08:11.590
Where is it?

08:14.400 --> 08:16.640
The ring isn't responding anymore.

08:18.990 --> 08:20.390
It's there!

08:37.040 --> 08:39.070
I can't reach it.

08:39.070 --> 08:41.320
A little bit more. Go for it!

08:47.560 --> 08:50.590
The star drops have an affinity to water, so...

08:50.590 --> 08:52.680
it must be chasing the rain.

09:01.780 --> 09:03.600
Aki- Sumomo!

09:04.690 --> 09:05.830
Yuki-chan.

09:07.280 --> 09:08.900
You're using my name.

09:10.020 --> 09:13.970
Are you okay? You look really wet too.

09:22.170 --> 09:24.280
Are you alright, Sumomo?

09:24.370 --> 09:25.470
N-Nako-chan.

09:27.150 --> 09:28.420
Sumomo!

09:29.150 --> 09:30.900
Nako-chan, watch out!

09:34.690 --> 09:35.670
For real?!

09:40.370 --> 09:42.860
Sumomo, use the chant.

09:44.520 --> 09:46.490
Puruvu Radi!

09:53.430 --> 09:54.600
I-I got it!

09:56.870 --> 10:01.710
I got it! Yuki-chan, I got it, the star drop!

10:06.800 --> 10:08.100
Oh noooo!

10:08.100 --> 10:09.960
Someone saw us!

10:11.080 --> 10:15.390
Sumomo, why don't you come by my house?

10:15.390 --> 10:18.590
You'll catch a cold with those wet clothes.

10:21.090 --> 10:22.290
Okay?

10:55.330 --> 10:56.580
Yaeno...

11:27.900 --> 11:29.750
Shall I clean your butt too?

11:29.760 --> 11:31.600
No thanks!

11:33.360 --> 11:36.450
That was you speaking, right?

11:39.970 --> 11:41.090
Yes.

11:42.000 --> 11:45.090
I see, so you can speak.

11:45.900 --> 11:48.320
I saw you moving and jumping around too.

11:49.130 --> 11:52.140
<i>S-She saw everything!</i>

11:53.390 --> 11:55.860
Nako-chan, that was a good bath.

11:56.480 --> 11:58.570
Do you feel better now?

11:58.690 --> 11:59.620
Yes.

12:02.200 --> 12:05.340
Did you clean those?

12:09.520 --> 12:11.840
What is this thing called?

12:13.050 --> 12:15.630
Sorry, she found out.

12:15.630 --> 12:21.170
Err, umm... I'm sorry, it's not that I wanted to hide Yuki-chan from you.

12:21.170 --> 12:22.460
So it's called Yuki-chan.

12:24.100 --> 12:26.970
It's already late now so shall we head out?

12:26.970 --> 12:29.420
Mom said she will drive you back home.

12:35.570 --> 12:38.240
Found it. Here it is.

12:39.940 --> 12:45.740
When a person from Retroscena sees a Spinear gathering star drops,

12:45.740 --> 12:48.700
that person's memory must be deleted.

12:49.420 --> 12:52.080
By using the Ladle to hit the person's head,

12:52.080 --> 12:59.600
the memory can be erased using the power from Figurare.

13:01.280 --> 13:03.010
Delete the memory...?

13:03.010 --> 13:05.870
Looks like we are okay...

13:08.310 --> 13:12.620
I can't do it; such a thing as deleting Nako-chan's memories...

13:13.670 --> 13:18.390
But you will only delete the memory about the incident.

13:18.390 --> 13:19.690
I can't do it...

13:20.640 --> 13:24.740
It's not like Nako-chan is going to forget about you...

13:26.490 --> 13:33.620
But the memory of Nako-chan cleaning these clothes will disappear...

13:35.280 --> 13:41.070
Nako-chan cleaned it carefully from top to bottom.

13:41.970 --> 13:46.070
Deleting such a kind feeling from her...

13:46.910 --> 13:48.410
I can't do it...

13:56.030 --> 14:03.590
kisetsu no nagare wa dare ni mo tomerarezu

13:56.030 --> 14:03.590
No one can stop the flow of the season

14:00.750 --> 14:03.350
We've always been together...

14:03.510 --> 14:05.840
Since we were little.

14:06.120 --> 14:09.310
Nako-chan was always there for me.

14:06.270 --> 14:13.890
watashino kokoro mo sono mama nagararete

14:06.270 --> 14:13.890
It's similar to that my heart also keeps flowing

14:09.550 --> 14:13.620
Always taking care of me.

14:16.510 --> 14:24.050
moshikashitara daijina koto kizukazuni

14:16.510 --> 14:24.050
Maybe I missed something important

14:25.720 --> 14:33.120
itanokamo shirenai gomenne

14:25.720 --> 14:33.120
If I did I'm sorry

14:36.870 --> 14:41.600
hitori de sabishi toki mo

14:36.870 --> 14:41.600
When I'm along and feel lonely

14:41.970 --> 14:46.500
hitori de kanashii toki mo

14:41.970 --> 14:46.500
When I'm alone and feel sad

14:47.110 --> 14:51.810
watashi no soba ni anata ga

14:47.110 --> 14:51.810
You are there beside me

14:50.970 --> 14:52.600
<i>Sumomo...</i>

14:52.230 --> 14:56.920
itsumo itsumo itekureta

14:52.230 --> 14:56.920
Always always there for me

14:56.900 --> 14:58.930
But I...

14:57.260 --> 15:01.750
isshouni waratteitte kureta

14:57.260 --> 15:01.750
We laughed together

14:58.930 --> 15:00.830
I can't do it.

15:01.210 --> 15:02.370
Sumomo...

15:02.470 --> 15:06.930
isshouni naite kureta ne

15:02.470 --> 15:06.930
Cried together

15:07.520 --> 15:11.400
watashi wo shinjite kureta

15:07.520 --> 15:11.400
You believed in me

15:11.610 --> 15:16.350
soba ni ite kureta

15:11.610 --> 15:16.350
Being there beside me

15:19.730 --> 15:23.900
With the Gardening Club privilege, I'm going to take a Hydrangea flower.

15:25.390 --> 15:26.310
Okay.

15:30.940 --> 15:31.990
Sumomo?

15:31.990 --> 15:32.690
Eh?

15:38.960 --> 15:40.920
<i>Things seem awkward between them. </i>

15:40.920 --> 15:43.100
<i>Must be because of what happened yesterday. </i>

15:48.610 --> 15:50.340
I have a favor to ask you.

15:51.390 --> 15:55.110
Can you walk Sumomo home today?

15:55.110 --> 15:55.980
Huh?

15:55.980 --> 15:57.880
Me with Akihime?

15:59.310 --> 16:00.730
How about you, Nako-chan?

16:01.510 --> 16:05.480
I have to stop by somewhere to take care of something for my mother.

16:07.660 --> 16:10.380
Don't push yourself like yesterday, okay?

16:10.380 --> 16:12.240
Or you'll catch a cold.

16:12.720 --> 16:15.540
Tsuwabuki, I'm counting on you.

16:15.540 --> 16:16.490
Okay.

16:53.250 --> 16:55.500
It's raining.

17:02.570 --> 17:05.000
I-I'm sorry.

17:34.230 --> 17:35.650
Umm...

17:35.650 --> 17:37.480
Y-Yes?

17:37.480 --> 17:40.060
Just talk normally.

17:41.350 --> 17:44.200
Just a normal answer is fine.

17:44.200 --> 17:46.650
Yes!

17:52.120 --> 17:53.120
Are you alright?

17:54.680 --> 17:57.330
Since you are different than usual, Akihime.

18:01.540 --> 18:02.800
What happened?

18:04.990 --> 18:11.340
Do you have a special friend, Tsuwabuki-kun?

18:14.360 --> 18:18.750
Someone that you've been with since you were young.

18:18.750 --> 18:21.080
And you talk about everything with her.

18:21.080 --> 18:24.430
Keeping no secrets.

18:24.430 --> 18:26.880
A really important friend.

18:29.890 --> 18:31.690
Umm...

18:31.690 --> 18:34.050
Continue on with the story.

18:36.090 --> 18:40.950
With such an important friend like that,

18:40.950 --> 18:46.110
you shouldn't lie or something like that, right?

18:59.840 --> 19:01.850
You can, maybe...

19:01.850 --> 19:02.950
Eh?

19:03.320 --> 19:06.690
Because lies come in different types.

19:08.150 --> 19:11.960
You treasure your friend very much, right?

19:13.620 --> 19:15.940
Then I think everything is fine.

19:21.380 --> 19:24.410
Sorry, I can't say it any better.

19:31.020 --> 19:32.630
Escorting you this far is fine, right?

19:32.630 --> 19:35.280
I have to get back now.

19:35.280 --> 19:36.360
Later.

19:38.420 --> 19:40.560
Tsuwabuki-kun...

19:45.370 --> 19:48.480
This is strange, I'm not transforming.

19:49.880 --> 19:52.350
The sun should have gone down already.

19:52.860 --> 19:53.880
Tonight is...?

19:54.420 --> 19:57.770
During the new moon, you will not transform.

19:57.770 --> 20:00.230
You will stay your human form the whole day.

20:01.260 --> 20:02.710
New moon...

20:10.770 --> 20:12.230
Kisaragi-sensei!

20:16.710 --> 20:20.190
Of course, he is not here anymore.

20:20.950 --> 20:24.360
Is there any other way without erasing Yaeno's memory?

20:25.070 --> 20:27.770
I'm thinking Sensei might have an idea.

20:28.930 --> 20:32.430
Damn it! What can I do?!

20:55.460 --> 20:57.610
Ah, I see!

21:05.490 --> 21:09.350
Sumomo-chan, you got a letter.

21:10.300 --> 21:14.870
I'm sorry, tonight I cannot go to Sumomo's place.

21:14.870 --> 21:17.450
But I found this in the book.

21:17.450 --> 21:20.880
A way so that we don't have to erase Nako-chan's memory.

21:21.500 --> 21:27.340
If you two truly believe in each other then telling the secret is permitted.

21:27.580 --> 21:29.370
To only one person.

21:31.160 --> 21:35.370
Listen, chant this while holding Nako-chan's hand.

21:35.710 --> 21:37.520
Ruaro

21:39.510 --> 21:44.110
If Sumomo-chan and Nako-chan truly believe in each other then...

21:44.380 --> 21:46.350
...a mark will appear.

22:10.040 --> 22:13.100
<i>On the next day I found it.</i>

22:14.210 --> 22:17.840
<i>The mark of a believer. </i>

22:23.170 --> 22:28.610
<i>I wonder why I feel so surprisingly relieved. </i>

22:51.680 --> 22:55.220
kira kira no hoshikuzu ha maru de

22:51.680 --> 22:55.220
Fragments of glittering stars

22:55.220 --> 22:58.520
koi suru otome no kiseki

22:55.220 --> 22:58.520
are just like the miracles of a girl in love

22:58.770 --> 23:02.310
kinou mada no watashi ha doko he

22:58.770 --> 23:02.310
Where did the cleverness from yesterday go,

23:02.310 --> 23:05.230
nanika chigau RABIRINSU

23:02.310 --> 23:05.230
Since it's like a labyrinth now

23:05.730 --> 23:09.490
dan dan wakan naku naru

23:05.730 --> 23:09.490
Slowly becoming confused

23:09.650 --> 23:12.490
（doushi you　doushi you）

23:09.650 --> 23:12.490
What do I do? What do I do?

23:12.740 --> 23:19.710
don don afurete kuru　AH　HAHAHA

23:12.740 --> 23:19.710
Slowly becoming overflowed

23:19.870 --> 23:25.590
yume no naka jya　nandemo ieru no ni…

23:19.870 --> 23:25.590
But inside a dream, can't you say anything?

23:25.590 --> 23:29.220
yuuki kudasai

23:25.590 --> 23:29.220
Please give me courage

23:30.510 --> 23:32.140
mo-o！

23:30.510 --> 23:32.140
Mo-o!

23:32.300 --> 23:36.970
konna ni aitai no ni

23:32.300 --> 23:36.970
I really want to meet you

23:36.970 --> 23:39.270
kanari Bi-myo

23:36.970 --> 23:39.270
Proxy doll

23:39.430 --> 23:43.190
toki meki ga koi no saidai no teki

23:39.430 --> 23:43.190
This throbbing is love's biggest challenge

23:43.190 --> 23:44.770
jirettai no yo

23:43.190 --> 23:44.770
It's irritating

23:44.770 --> 23:46.110
ne-e

23:44.770 --> 23:46.110
Isn't it?

23:46.520 --> 23:51.240
yume kara sametara mata

23:46.520 --> 23:51.240
The reasons to wake again

23:51.240 --> 23:56.780
kobore souna kimi no egao ni

23:51.240 --> 23:56.780
Are overflowing to see your smile

23:56.780 --> 23:59.700
airu kana

23:56.780 --> 23:59.700
If we meet again

24:10.250 --> 24:11.680
During Tanabata...

24:10.880 --> 24:12.550
Next Episode

24:11.680 --> 24:13.200
Why does it rain every year?

24:13.400 --> 24:15.640
Even when it's a day for lovers.

24:15.640 --> 24:16.450
That's why it rains.

24:16.450 --> 24:17.060
What?!

24:17.060 --> 24:19.240
Speaking of which, on Tanabata a transfer student came.

24:19.240 --> 24:20.130
What kind of person?

24:20.130 --> 24:20.610
Beautiful girl?

24:21.380 --> 24:22.810
Love at first sight with me!

24:21.520 --> 24:25.020
Episode 3

24:21.520 --> 24:25.020
Golden Wishing Star

24:23.280 --> 24:23.770
That...

24:23.760 --> 24:25.020
won't happen.
